/T (Feature importance and SHAP analysis identified that timestamp-derived features \(FLOW_START_MILLISECONDS / FLOW_END_MILLISECONDS\) carried the largest single feature-importance share, with severe distributional drift between datasets. In effect, the model was substantially learning which lab environment generated a given flow rather than whether that flow was malicious.)
/E (Feature importance and SHAP analysis identified that timestamp-derived features \(FLOW_START_MILLISECONDS / FLOW_END_MILLISECONDS\) carried the largest single feature-importance share, with severe distributional drift between datasets. In effect, the model was substantially learning which lab environment generated a given flow rather than whether that flow was malicious.)
